  "description": "DARKOA crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C88 H108 Br8 Dy4 N8 Ni8 O36,3.25(C2 H6 O1),4(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni4 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni5 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni6 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni7 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni8 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.077-3.935 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 82.46-113.96°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy4Ni8(μ3-OH)8(L)8(OAc)4(H2O)4]·3.25EtOH·4CH3CN (L = 4-bromo-2-[(2-hydroxypropylimino)methyl]phenolate; EA C102.5H139.5Br8Dy4N12Ni8O39.25). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
